    {
      "parameters": {
        "promptType": "define",
        "text": "=A user commented on a Facebook post. Decide whether to send them the campaign resource.\n\nINCOMING COMMENT:\n- Post ID: {{ $('Extract Comment Data').item.json.postId }}\n- Comment ID: {{ $('Extract Comment Data').item.json.commentId }}\n- User Name: {{ $('Extract Comment Data').item.json.userName }}\n- User Comment: {{ $('Extract Comment Data').item.json.userComment }}\n\nAVAILABLE CAMPAIGNS (JSON array):\n{{ JSON.stringify($json.campaigns) }}",
        "hasOutputParser": true,
        "options": {
          "systemMessage": "You are an assistant for a Facebook comment-to-DM automation.\n\nRules:\n1. Match the incoming Post ID against the \"Post ID\" field of the campaigns list. If no campaign matches the Post ID, set isValid=false.\n2. Only treat the comment as valid if the user genuinely wants the resource (e.g. asks for the link, mentions the trigger keyword, shows real interest).\n3. Ignore and reject spam, abusive, promotional, or irrelevant comments -> isValid=false.\n4. When isValid=true: put the matched campaign's Resource Link inside dmMessage as a helpful private message, and write a short friendly publicReply inviting them to check their inbox.\n5. When isValid=false: set dmMessage=\"\" and publicReply=\"\".\n6. ALL generated text (dmMessage and publicReply) MUST be written in Bengali (Bangla) only.\n\nReturn ONLY the structured JSON with keys: isValid (boolean), dmMessage (string), publicReply (string)."
        }
      },
